[{:adr/consequences ["https://api.murakumo.cloud/infer/hwmetrics/ui shows live per-node CPU/GPU/mem/disk for gad + the Apple M4\n   mesh, auto-refreshing every 5s, offline nodes clearly badged instead of silently missing" "surfaces a previously-invisible operational fact: the inference workers are concurrently mining Monero\n   (xmrig), so their near-saturated CPU numbers are real contention, not idle headroom" "the collector script is the first hardware-utilization telemetry in either repo — prior /itonami/perf and\n   /infer/fleet were static/anonymized; this is the pattern to extend if per-node GPU tok/s or per-request\n   attribution is wanted later"], :adr/repos ["orgs/kotoba-lang/murakumo" "orgs/gftdcojp/local-murakumo"], :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607051431-murakumo-cloud-live-inference-anthropic-bridge.md"], :adr/status "closed", :adr/id "adr-2607051730-murakumo-cloud-fleet-hwmetrics-dashboard", :adr/follow-ups-not-done ["no historical retention/sparklines — only the single latest snapshot is stored (KV doc, not a stream);\n   would need a bounded ring buffer if trend charts are wanted" "hwmetrics-report.sh's WORKERS array duplicates fleet.edn's :host list by hand — could be generated at\n   `nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs`-adjacent tooling time instead of maintained by hand" "no alerting (e.g. a node flapping offline/online) — dashboard is read-only visualization, not monitoring"], :adr/addendum-2026-07-05-part1-gpu-default "{:change \"swapped GPU above CPU in both the SSR card (local-murakumo.infer-view/node-card) and the live\\n          JS poller's renderNode — GPU renders first now, CPU second\", :reason \"GPU is the meaningful utilization signal for an inference fleet; CPU is dominated by the\\n          concurrent xmrig mining load noted in decision :2-collector above, so leading with CPU was\\n          visually prioritizing the less relevant number\", :repo \"orgs/gftdcojp/local-murakumo — no schema/route change, pure view-ordering fix\"}", :adr/date "2026-07-05", :adr/decisions "{:1-precision-and-placement {:question \"how precise, and where does the collector run?\", :user-choice {:precision \"full precision via powermetrics/root (not a no-root approximation)\", :placement \"background daemon on gad (not an on-demand manual command)\", :access \"public read (matches existing /itonami/perf, /infer/fleet transparency posture); write side token-gated\"}, :prereq-check \"passwordless sudo for `powermetrics` already provisioned on every Apple M4 mesh node —\\n                  no new sudoers change needed. gad already holds SSH access to the whole mesh + the\\n                  cloudflared tunnel reaching api.murakumo.cloud, so it's the natural collector host.\"}, :2-collector {:new-file \"orgs/kotoba-lang/murakumo/tools/hwmetrics-report/hwmetrics-report.sh\", :gad-local \"CPU: 200ms /proc/stat delta (no root). GPU: /sys/class/drm/card1/device/{gpu_busy_percent,\\n              mem_info_vram_used,mem_info_vram_total} — amdgpu exposes these unprivileged. mem: free -b. disk: df -k /.\", :mac-workers \"one ssh round-trip per node: `sudo -n powermetrics -n1 -i1000 --samplers cpu_power,gpu_power`\\n                (real E-Cluster/P-Cluster + GPU HW active residency) + vm_stat/sysctl/df. CPU% = core-count-\\n                weighted average of E/P cluster active residency.\", :concurrency-bug-caught-before-shipping {:found \"serial SSH against fleet.edn's 10-node roster (4 of which are routinely offline/asleep) costs\\n           4×ConnectTimeout=16s alone — 21s measured wall-clock total, blowing past any sane report interval\", :fix \"all ~11 probes (gad + 10 workers) run concurrently as background jobs, collected via a tmpdir + wait;\\n         measured wall-clock dropped to ~2-4s\"}, :surprise-finding \"worker CPU% reads ~90-100% on every node, consistently, across repeated samples — initially\\n                      suspected as a powermetrics short-sample measurement artifact (HW active residency ≠ Unix\\n                      CPU-idle%), but `top -l` confirmed the same ~90-100% independently: the same 10 Apple M4\\n                      minis (fleet.edn) also run `xmrig` as a standing Monero-mining fleet (see the `uriage`\\n                      skill) — genuinely real, continuous CPU load, not a bug. Exactly the kind of contention\\n                      this dashboard is meant to surface.\", :roster \"WORKERS array is a static mirror of fleet.edn's :host list — fleet.edn stays the SSoT, both need\\n           updating together if the mesh roster changes.\"}, :3-api-and-dashboard {:repo \"orgs/gftdcojp/local-murakumo\", :routes {:post \"/infer/hwmetrics — Bearer MURAKUMO_METRICS_TOKEN gated (worker.cljs-only; the pure\\n                  routes.cljc layer has no header/env access, matching how /v1/messages auth also lives\\n                  only in worker.cljs). Overwrites a single `hwmetrics/latest` doc via IStore -put/-get —\\n                  NOT an append-only stream like /infer/fleet, since the collector posts every ~10s forever\\n                  and only the current reading is ever shown.\", :get \"/infer/hwmetrics — public JSON, latest snapshot\", :get-ui \"/infer/hwmetrics/ui — public SSR page (local-murakumo.infer-view/fleet-page), inline\\n                    vanilla-JS poller (5s, no reagent/re-frame — this page has its own independent poll loop\\n                    over different state than /infer/ui's model-centric app; duplicating ~20 lines of render\\n                    logic in JS was simpler than threading a second state slice through the existing\\n                    single-page re-frame app)\"}, :tested \"routes.cljc covered by a new JVM test (hwmetrics deftest: no-report-yet, POST overwrite semantics,\\n           /ui rendering incl. offline badge) — 26 tests / 202 assertions all green\"}, :4-secret-provisioning {:token \"MURAKUMO_METRICS_TOKEN, openssl rand -hex 32\", :stored [\"1Password gftd.murakumo/METRICS_TOKEN (vault gftdcojp, API Credential category)\" \"Cloudflare Worker secret via `wrangler secret put`\" \"root-only /etc/murakumo-hwmetrics.env (mode 600) on gad, read by the systemd unit's EnvironmentFile\"]}, :5-systemd-on-gad {:script-path \"/home/gad/murakumo/hwmetrics-report.sh\", :unit \"murakumo-hwmetrics.service (oneshot) + murakumo-hwmetrics.timer (OnBootSec 15s, OnUnitActiveSec 10s)\", :verified \"systemctl enable --now; journalctl confirmed clean 10s-interval runs (initial 404s before the\\n             Worker deploy landed, 201s after)\"}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:ask \"visualize live CPU/GPU/storage utilization for the gad + murakumo fleet on murakumo.cloud in realtime\", :found \"no hardware-metrics collection existed at all — murakumo.infer/probe-node only reads mem/disk totals over SSH\\n          (sysctl hw.memsize, df, iogpu.wired_limit_mb), never utilization %; /itonami/perf is hardcoded benchmark\\n          data, not live; /infer/fleet is an anonymized append-only stream with no live producer\"}", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "murakumo.cloud — live CPU/GPU/mem/disk fleet dashboard", :adr/addendum-2026-07-05-part2-offline-node-investigation "{:trigger \"user asked why dan/joseph/levi/simeon show offline on the dashboard\", :method \"direct SSH from this machine timed out for all four (consistent with the dashboard's\\n          reachable:false), then cross-checked against `tailscale status` independently of the\\n          hwmetrics collector/SSH path entirely\", :finding \"all four show `offline, last seen 1d ago` in tailscale status itself — genuinely powered\\n           off/asleep at the network layer, not an SSH quirk or a dashboard bug. The other 6 mesh nodes\\n           (asher, benjamin, gad, issachar, judah, naphtali, zebulun) show active/reachable.\", :verdict \"dashboard is reporting correctly; this reconfirms decision :1-precision-and-placement's\\n           and ADR-2607051431's existing note that not all 10 fleet.edn nodes are kept awake at once —\\n           no fix needed, no bug\"}"}]